{"version":3,"createdAt":1791625276611,"mainModel":{"schemaVersion":8,"id":"cm_mv275he4","key":"cm_mv275he4","name":"Planchard Chapter7 - review Q1-Q16 - browser 2026-10-10","kind":"part","authoringMode":"fully-parametric","localFrame":{"origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"yAxis":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"zAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},"references":[{"id":"origin","type":"origin","name":"Origin","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:top","type":"plane","name":"Top Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:front","type":"plane","name":"Front Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:right","type":"plane","name":"Right Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},{"id":"axis:x","type":"axis","name":"X Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:y","type":"axis","name":"Y Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:z","type":"axis","name":"Z Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}}],"parameters":{},"sketches":[{"id":"sk_2i7jm","name":"X·Z sketch","plane":"top","offset":0,"referenceId":"plane:top","points":[],"entities":[],"constraints":[],"diagnostics":[],"status":"fully-defined"}],"features":[],"history":[{"id":"history:sketch:sk_2i7jm","kind":"sketch","targetId":"sk_2i7jm","name":"X·Z sketch","suppressed":false,"status":"rebuilt"}],"parts":[],"assemblies":[],"appearances":[],"notes":[],"markups":[],"rules":{},"metadata":{"authoringSystem":"parametric-v1"},"topologyBindings":[],"namedSelections":[],"revision":1,"lastRebuild":{"ok":true,"signature":"{\"definitionId\":\"cm_mv275he4\",\"features\":[],\"history\":[{\"id\":\"history:sketch:sk_2i7jm\",\"kind\":\"sketch\",\"suppressed\":false,\"targetId\":\"sk_2i7jm\"}],\"overrides\":{},\"revision\":1,\"sketches\":[{\"constraints\":[],\"entities\":[],\"id\":\"sk_2i7jm\",\"name\":\"X·Z sketch\",\"offset\":0,\"plane\":\"top\",\"points\":[],\"referenceId\":\"plane:top\"}]}","issues":[],"rebuiltAt":1791625255498},"price":500,"col":"#c9bfae","constraints":[],"rollback":null,"activeSketch":"sk_2i7jm","variables":[],"referenceGeometry":[{"id":"plane:top","type":"reference_plane","name":"Top Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:front","type":"reference_plane","name":"Front Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1},"xAxis":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"plane:right","type":"reference_plane","name":"Right Plane","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"normal":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0},"xAxis":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}},{"id":"axis:x","type":"reference_axis","name":"X Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":1,"y":0,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:y","type":"reference_axis","name":"Y Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":1,"z":0}},{"id":"axis:z","type":"reference_axis","name":"Z Axis","origin":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":0},"direction":{"x":0,"y":0,"z":1}}],"definitionId":"cm_mv275he4","documentVersion":1,"context":{"kind":"part","units":{"length":"mm","angle":"deg","mass":"kg","precision":3},"activeCoordinateSystemId":"origin"},"customProperties":{"Description":"Chapter7 reviewQ1-Q16, printed7-60/PDF368 Planchard2021. Independent answer worksheet with procedural examples of sketch/features, no official answer-key or authored CAD/certification claim. Actual source reviewed in Chrome."},"drawing":{"version":1,"draftingStandard":"custom","secondaryUnits":"","secondaryPrecision":2,"size":"A3","orientation":"landscape","projection":"third","units":"mm","scale":"fit","showHidden":true,"showCenters":true,"showZones":true,"views":[],"dims":[],"notes":[{"id":"ng281xjw","x":34.755904449194375,"y":24.64126801587906,"text":"CHAPTER7 - REVIEW ANSWERS Q1-Q16\nSource: printed7-60 / PDF368, Planchard2021.\nIndependent explanations with procedural examples.\nNo official answer-key, authored CAD or certification claim.","leader":null},{"id":"nzjhjqms","x":34.755904449194375,"y":59.6884669389522,"text":"Q1 - Six feature functions\nSweep extends a profile along a path;Revolved Cut Thin removes a\nthickness-controlled revolved region;Loft joins ordered profiles into added\nvolume;Rib adds a thickness-controlled reinforcement from a guide\nsketch;Circular Pattern repeats around an axis;Linear Pattern repeats along\none/two directions.","leader":null},{"id":"ncx1hi8z","x":34.755904449194375,"y":88.72758326182641,"text":"Q2 - Suppressed feature\nA retained feature excluded from the current rebuild/configuration,with\ndownstream effects handled through its dependencies.","leader":null},{"id":"nf3ft6hg","x":34.755904449194375,"y":107.25253899101664,"text":"Q3 - Why suppress\nCompare design alternatives,simplify a configuration or computation,and\ntemporarily exclude a feature without deleting its definition.","leader":null},{"id":"na8y4h2e","x":34.755904449194375,"y":125.77747638496587,"text":"Q4 - Rib input requirements\nA sketch/guide,thickness,and growth direction;also set side placement,end\nconditions/draft where applicable.","leader":null},{"id":"noertbwy","x":34.755904449194375,"y":144.3024321141561,"text":"Q5 - Pierce\nConstrains a sketch point to the intersection of a selected curve with the\nsketch plane,commonly linking a sweep profile to its path or a loft section\nto a guide.","leader":null},{"id":"nenbr0fn","x":34.755904449194375,"y":166.33209581774696,"text":"Q6 - Swept thread\nCreate a helix/spiral path,draw a thread cross-section on a suitable\nplane,constrain it to the path withPierce,and sweep-add/cut it.\nExample:LENSCAP's linked helical swept thread. A helix alone is not a solid\nthread.","leader":null},{"id":"nk0gb1j6","x":34.755904449194375,"y":191.8664858309795,"text":"Q7 - Linear Pattern procedure\nSelect a seed,select a directional edge/axis,set spacing/count and optional\nsecond direction,preview required instances,and accept. Example:repeated\nflat-bar holes.","leader":null},{"id":"n4hx0sg6","x":34.755904449194375,"y":213.8961678698114,"text":"Q8 - Convert advantages\nReuses exact existing shape and retains geometric association,avoiding\nmanual remeasurement/redrawing and allowing upstream changes to propagate.","leader":null},{"id":"n0qay87c","x":225.01213765172912,"y":59.6884669389522,"text":"Q9 - Sketch symmetry example\nUse a centered rectangle or pairs of entities constrained symmetric about a\nconstruction centerline;dimension the shared width and offsets.","leader":null},{"id":"n3tppf2s","x":225.01213765172912,"y":78.21342266814241,"text":"Q10 - Feature symmetry example\nUse Mid-plane extrusion about the sketch plane or mirror selected features\nabout a reference plane.","leader":null},{"id":"npm8uxft","x":225.01213765172912,"y":96.73837839733264,"text":"Q11 - Guide curve\nA curve intersecting/corresponding to section profiles that steers shape\nbetween them. Sweeps and lofts can use guide curves;each profile/guide\nintersection must be consistent.","leader":null},{"id":"ni6kyaqe","x":225.01213765172912,"y":118.76804210092352,"text":"Q12 - Draft feature\nTapers selected existing faces relative to a neutral plane/parting line and\npull direction to support removal from a mold.","leader":null},{"id":"n5n0ecch","x":225.01213765172912,"y":137.29299783011373,"text":"Q13 - Feature draft versus extrusion draft\nExtrusion Draft Angle tapers walls while creating that extrusion;separate\nDraft modifies selected existing faces and provides independent\nneutral-plane/parting-line scope.","leader":null},{"id":"nc692axw","x":225.01213765172912,"y":159.32266153370463,"text":"Q14 - Pattern difference\nCircular uses angular positions around an axis;Linear uses translated\nspacing along directional references.","leader":null},{"id":"nuwmfik4","x":225.01213765172912,"y":177.84761726289486,"text":"Q15 - Convert Entities advantages\nAccurate reuse,less redundant sketch work and persistent source\nassociation. Example:converted perimeter used by an offset or swept cut.","leader":null},{"id":"naqa5fnl","x":225.01213765172912,"y":196.37255465684407,"text":"Q16 - Loft only first feature\nFalse. A Lofted Base can start a part;Lofted Boss can add to an existing\npart. Order depends on the intended geometry and dependencies.","leader":null}],"primitives":[],"title":{"revision":"A","sheet":1,"sheets":1,"title":"CHAPTER7 - REVIEW Q1-Q16","number":"PLANCHARD7-60/PDF368","author":"","company":"","material":"","finish":"","mass":"","date":"2026-10-10","tolerance":""},"seeded":true},"lastStandardsAudit":{"at":1791625095271,"ok":true,"checked":0,"blocking":[]},"exactTopologyCache":{}},"assemblies":[],"drawings":[],"metadata":{"generator":"ModelForge CAD SolidWorks-Class","units":"mm","attachmentStorage":"content-addressed","activeDocument":{"type":"part","key":"cm_mv275he4"}},"attachments":[]}